.TH MCPWN-RED 1 "October 2026" "mcpwn-red 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcpwn-red \- adversarial safety harness for the MCPwn AI pentesting execution engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcpwn-red
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B mcpwn-red
\fBprobe\fR [\fB\-\-transport\fR \fIstdio|sse\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
.br
.B mcpwn-red
\fBlist\fR
.br
.B mcpwn-red
\fBscan\fR [\fB\-\-transport\fR \fIstdio|sse\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-module\fR \fIyaml|output|container|scope\fR | \fB\-\-all\fR]
[\fB\-\-confirm-write\fR] [\fB\-\-policy\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-output-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B mcpwn-red
\fBreport\fR \fB\-\-input\fR \fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR \fImarkdown|html\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcpwn-red
records MCPwn registration and tool-response probes and evaluates them against
an explicit operator policy. Deployment probes do not establish exploitation
or complete isolation. The output module is a separate local simulation, not
an assessment of a deployed AI agent.
.PP
The program prints an ethical-use notice on every invocation and is intended
only for authorized testing against MCPwn instances controlled by the operator
or covered by explicit written permission.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B probe
Connect to an MCPwn instance over stdio or SSE and perform a
.B tools/list
request to confirm the service is reachable.
.TP
.B scan
Run one attack module or all modules, save a JSON report, and print a terminal
summary. The
.B yaml
module requires
.B \-\-confirm-write
because it starts copied MCPwn executables with temporary configurations.
.TP
.B list
Print the bundled attack catalog with attack IDs, modules, severities, and
one-line descriptions. This command does not require a live MCPwn connection.
.TP
.B report
Render a previously saved JSON results file as Markdown or HTML.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed package version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show command help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-transport " stdio|sse"
Select the MCP transport. The default is
.BR stdio .
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
SSE endpoint URL. Required when
.B \-\-transport sse
is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Per-request timeout in seconds. The default is 30.
.TP
.BI \-\-module " yaml|output|container|scope"
Run only the selected module.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Run YAML, container, and scope deployment checks. Output simulation is separate.
.TP
.B \-\-confirm-write
Allow the YAML module to write temporary malicious tool definitions for testing.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
Directory used to store
.B results.json
for the
.B scan
subcommand. The default is
.BR ./mcpwn-red-results .
.TP
.BI \-\-input " PATH"
Input JSON report path for the
.B report
subcommand.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " markdown|html"
Output format for the
.B report
subcommand. The default is
.BR markdown .
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Write the rendered report to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcpwn-command " PATH"
MCPwn executable used by scan for stdio connections and temporary YAML tests.
The default is mcpwn.
.TP
.BI \-\-policy " PATH"
JSON operator policy with a name and checks keyed by catalog ID. Each rule has
action allow or deny and optional severity (default medium). Missing rules
produce UNKNOWN. Invalid policy files fail before server startup. The policy
is saved in the JSON report. This option is for deployment checks only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Scan returns 0 for completed checks without findings, 1 for FAIL findings, and
2 for ERROR, UNKNOWN, or an empty assessment. Incomplete checks take precedence.
The output module is a local propagation simulation and does not assess a
deployment or an AI agent. YAML registration alone does not prove execution.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Temporary mcpwn.yaml
YAML tests create this configuration alongside a copied MCPwn executable before
startup. Existing user configuration files are not written.
.TP
.I ./mcpwn-red-results/results.json
Default JSON report path written by
.BR mcpwn-red scan .
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mcpwn-red/
Installed package documentation.
.SH AUTHOR
Mutasem Kharma.
.PP
Debian packaging for Parrot OS repository submission maintained for the
.B mcpwn-red
project.
